# Validation 3: set the Claude subscription as the AI model, the way a player does: from the watch, with one button.
# The Magician is the AI wish mode. The watch's "Turn on the Magician" opens the Magician
# setup; "Use my Claude subscription" picks Opus 5.5 for wishes and Haiku 5.5 as the helper, both paid for by Claude
# Code's own sign-in (no API key), and starts the setup at once: it checks Claude Code is installed and signed in,
# then runs the Magician check (real calls to the models, ending in one small test wish), about 3 minutes, once.
# Only a passed check turns the Magician on. The choice and the passed check are saved in Moddy's home folder, so 04
# and 05 build on them (validate.sh runs the set in order).
# Needs: Claude Code installed and signed in on this Mac (run `claude` once and sign in).
@intent From the watch, one button sets up the Magician on the Claude subscription, and its check turns it on

@step a clear stage
gamemode creative
time set noon
weather clear
gamerule advance_time false
gamerule spawn_mobs false
tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 10

@step open the watch
# The watch sits in the selected hotbar slot; using it opens the wish screen. The Magician is off for a new player.
@key key.use
@expect screen /make a wish/ within 10s
@wait 1s
@shot watch-magician-off

@step press "Turn on the Magician"
@click button "Turn on the Magician"
@expect screen Magician setup within 10s
@wait 1s
@shot magician-setup

@step choose the Claude subscription
@click item "Use my Claude subscription"
@expect chat /setting up the magician with your claude subscription/ within 10s
@expect actionbar /magician setup 1\/3/ within 20s
@shot checking-claude-code
@expect actionbar /magician setup 2\/3/ within 120s
@shot magician-check-running

@step the check passes and the Magician is on
# The check's last step is a real wish made by the wish model; allow it 10 minutes.
@expect chat /the magician is on: opus 5\.5 on your claude subscription/ within 600s
@wait 2s
@shot magician-on
